assuming you re trying to implement a write through cache say dcache the popular way out
is to use a write buffer.


writes from LSU go and check if dcache has the cacheline. if yes update in place and thats it

if dcache doesnt have it queue it in the write buffer and thats it

------------------------------------
writebuffer is flushed asynchronously first updates L2 (thereby respecting coherence) 
and then dcache.  Of course you could choose to not update dcache and let it fill up
on a read miss. (inclusive cache vs exclusive cache)


------------------------------------
what happens while wbuf has entries if a read operation comes along.

nothing do the same thing. check if the entry is in dcache. if it is its not in wbuf. return
this and you ll be safe.

if its not in dcache wait for wbuf flush and then read out of l2. at the same time allocate
a line in l1 that is filled with data once l2 returns. a few of these operations can be
interleaved but you ll still have coherence across different processors.


